# Codegen golden fixtures are byte-compared against fixpp-codegen output, which
# is always written with LF (main.cpp opens the output stream std::ios::binary).
# Pin them to LF so a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true on the windows-latest
# runners) does not CRLF-convert them and break the byte-exact determinism gate
# (tests/codegen/determinism_test.cpp — DeterminismTest.GeneratedMatchesGolden).
*.golden.hpp -text

# 074-orchestra-native-reader: the vendored FIX Orchestra source is pinned by a
# byte-exact sha1 supply-chain gate (tests/dictionary/CMakeLists.txt file(SHA1)
# vs 26f60db1…). A Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true on the windows-msvc
# runners) CRLF-converts it → different bytes → different sha1 → the gate
# FATAL_ERRORs at configure. Pin it to LF so it is byte-identical on all
# platforms (same class as the golden fixtures above).
dictionaries/orchestra/OrchestraFIXLatest.xml -text

# 075-live-wire-enum-validation: the enum-golden manifest gate raw-byte-SHA1s
# these vendored/pinned text files (tests/wire/enum_golden_manifest_test.cpp
# DictionarySha1{Fix44,Fix41,Fix42}Matches + GeneratorSourceHashMatches). A
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true on the windows-msvc runners) CRLF-converts
# them → different bytes → different sha1 → the manifest test fails (it passed
# locally only because the rsync-populated MSVC sandbox carries LF files, which
# cannot reproduce a real Windows git checkout). Pin to LF (same class as above).
dictionaries/FIX44.xml -text
dictionaries/FIX41.xml -text
dictionaries/FIX42.xml -text
tools/quickfix_enum_golden/main.cpp -text
tools/quickfix_enum_golden/golden.csv -text

# 079-required-presence-scope T018: same CRLF-hash trap as above — the
# generator's manifest block SHA1s tools/quickfix_required_golden/main.cpp
# itself (generator_source_hash) and golden.csv is regenerated/diffed
# byte-for-byte by regen_and_diff.py. Pin to LF (main.cpp opens the output
# stream std::ios::binary, so a Windows checkout would otherwise CRLF-convert
# only the checked-in copy, not a freshly regenerated one).
tools/quickfix_required_golden/main.cpp -text
tools/quickfix_required_golden/golden.csv -text
# 081-strict-validation-residuals T020: the new per-group golden shares the
# same CRLF trap — pin to LF so a Windows checkout does not diverge the
# checked-in copy from a freshly regenerated one (generator opens the stream
# std::ios::binary) and no git-cleanliness gate reds on a CRLF-converted copy.
tools/quickfix_required_golden/golden_groups.csv -text
